  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kosovo Adapt Activity_USAID</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kosovo Adapt Activity_USAID</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADAPT contribution is a new collaboration h with USAID&#x2019;s Kosovo ADAPT Activity, aimed at enhancing climate resilience through the Climate Innovation Fund (CIF). This initiative seeks to facilitate the introduction of climate-smart technologies and mobilize up to 6 million USD in investments from private sector to promote innovative, sustainable, and green solutions and supporting Kosovo&#x2019;s path toward greater resilience and making a meaningful contribution to climate adaptation efforts.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ADAPT-bidrag &#xe4;r ett nytt samarbete med USAID:s Kosovo ADAPT Activity, som syftar till att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra klimatmotst&#xe5;ndskraften genom Climate Innovation Fund (CIF). Detta initiativ syftar till att underl&#xe4;tta inf&#xf6;randet av klimatsmarta teknologier och mobilisera upp till 6 miljoner USD i investeringar fr&#xe5;n den privata sektorn f&#xf6;r att fr&#xe4;mja innovativa, h&#xe5;llbara och gr&#xf6;na l&#xf6;sningar och st&#xf6;dja Kosovos v&#xe4;g mot st&#xf6;rre motst&#xe5;ndskraft och ge ett meningsfullt bidrag till klimatanpassningsinsatser.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The USAID Kosovo Adapt Activity main objective is to support private sector, and research sector organizations in Kosovo to enhance adaptive capacity and resilience. Through collaboration, strategic communication efforts, and leveraging resources like the Climate Innovation Fund (CIF) with technical assistance, the proposed intervention seeks to strengthen Kosovo&apos;s ability to adapt to climate change and maintain a resilient inclusive economy.
Specific expected outcomes the proposed intervention outlines specific measurable outcomes that are expected by the end of the intervention: Catalyze the introduction of at least 25 new technologies. Facilitate at least $6 million in investment for climate change adaptation and mitigation.</narrative>
  </description>
